{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"signalingNaN","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default IEEE 754 behavior of operations involving a signaling NaN is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to raise the Invalid flag in the floating-point environment and return a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"quiet NaN."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Operations on types conforming to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FloatingPoint"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol should"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"support this behavior, but they might also support other options. For"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example, it would be reasonable to implement alternative operations in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which operating on a signaling NaN triggers a runtime error or results"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in a diagnostic for debugging purposes. Types that implement alternative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"behaviors for a signaling NaN must document the departure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other than these signaling operations, a signaling NaN behaves in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same manner as a quiet NaN."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/floatingpoint\/signalingnan"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}